          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"output\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"null\"\n    },\n    \"followUpQuestions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"jobId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"conversationId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"traceId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"supportingChunks\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"citations\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"nodes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"waitingToolCode\": {\n      \"type\": \"null\"\n    },\n    \"workflowCode\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"workflowVersion\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"workflowStatus\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"startDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"endTime\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"createDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"endDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"timeTaken\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"inputTokenCount\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"outputTokenCount\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": []\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1779841882709",
          "code": "GET_PRODUCTS",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get products",
            "sourceCode": "let result = [];\ntry {\n  // Access the output string from GET_PRODUCT_INFORMATION node\n  const outputString = $context.$nodes?.GET_PRODUCT_INFORMATION?.$output?.output || \"\";\n\n  // Parse the output string safely\n  const parsedOutput = JSON.parse(outputString);\n\n  // The parsed output is expected to be an array, get the first element's subscriptions\n  // Defensive checks for structure\n  if (Array.isArray(parsedOutput) && parsedOutput.length > 0) {\n    const firstEntry = parsedOutput[0];\n    if (firstEntry && Array.isArray(firstEntry.subscriptions)) {\n      result = firstEntry.subscriptions;\n    }\n  }\n} catch (error) {\n  // On error, return empty array\n  result = [];\n}\n\nreturn result;",
            "returnType": "array"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5477,
            "y": 8758
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779842346045"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1779842346045",
          "code": "ADD_PRODUCTS_SUMMARY",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Add Products Summary"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5477,
            "y": 8980
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775957079972"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776795798277_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Based on {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRODUCTS.$output.result}}, if there are no rows in it, return {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_ACCOUNT_SUMMARY.$output}} as it is. No change is needed.\n\nif there are rows in {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_ACCOUNT_SUMMARY.$output}}, then create one object based on the row as below:\n\n  subject: <Generate a short few words concise sentence based on PRODUCTGROUPNAME, TOTALVALUEAMOUNT, TOTALARR, {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRODUCTS.$output.result}}>\n  subtitle: <Generate 1 line professional short sentence showing the insight from {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRODUCTS.$output.result}}>\n  summary: <Consolidate the Products Owned from {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRODUCTS.$output.result}} and Display in 2 bullet points format it with markdown. Must be 2 bullet points only>\n  badgeText: <Consolidate Products Owned from {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRODUCTS.$output.result}} and Generate a badge text based on the count of products. For example, \"2 Products\">\n  variant: <info>\n\nOnce created, append this new object at the start of the rows to the output from {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_ACCOUNT_SUMMARY.$output}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Execution Widget"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5477,
            "y": 9202
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CARD"
              ],
              "customNotes": "<multiCardWidget>\n    <description>Displays multiple card-style alerts or updates in a single widget, using the same card metadata format repeated in an array.</description>\n    <schema>\n{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"required\": [\"cards\"],\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"layoutMode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\"default\", \"collapsed\", \"single-col\"],\n            \"description\": \"Optional layout behavior. default preserves the normal responsive behavior, collapsed forces two cards per row, and single-col forces one card per row.\"\n        },\n        \"cards\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"description\": \"Array of card metadata objects. Use one entry per card.\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"required\": [\"subject\", \"summary\"],\n                \"properties\": {\n                    \"subject\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\",\n                        \"description\": \"Clear, concise title (2-6 words typically)\"\n                    },\n                    \"subtitle\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\",\n                        \"description\": \"Secondary line shown directly below the title\"\n                    },\n                    \"summary\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\",\n                        \"description\": \"1-2 sentences of descriptive text (under 100 characters when possible)\"\n                    },\n                    \"status\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\",\n                        \"description\": \"Bottom status text shown beneath the summary and above links\"\n                    },\n                    \"statusPriority\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\",\n                        \"enum\": [\"alert\", \"warning\", \"medium\", \"success\"],\n                        \"description\": \"Color priority for the status text (alert: critical, warning: caution, medium: neutral, success: positive)\"\n                    },\n                    \"timestamp\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\",\n                        \"description\": \"Human-readable relative time (e.g., '5 min ago', 'Yesterday')\"\n                    },\n                    \"badgeText\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\",\n                        \"description\": \"Short label for categorization\"\n                    },\n                    \"link\": {\n                        \"type\": \"object\",\n                        \"properties\": {\n                            \"text\": {\n                                \"type\": \"string\",\n                                \"description\": \"Action-oriented button text (1-3 words)\"\n                            },\n                            \"action\": {\n                                \"type\": \"string\",\n                                \"description\": \"Identifier for what the link does (snake_case format)\"\n                            }\n                        }\n                    },\n                    \"additionalLink\": {\n                        \"type\": \"object\",\n                        \"properties\": {\n                            \"text\": {\n                                \"type\": \"string\",\n                                \"description\": \"Secondary action text (1-3 words)\"\n                            },\n                            \"action\": {\n                                \"type\": \"string\",\n                                \"description\": \"Identifier for the secondary action (snake_case format)\"\n                            }\n                        }\n                    },\n                    \"variant\": {\n                        \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n                        \"enum\": [\"error\", \"warning\", \"info\", null],\n                        \"description\": \"Visual styling variant (error: critical issues, warning: cautions, info: updates, null: neutral)\"\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n    </schema>\n    <instructions>\nUse multiCardWidget when you need to show multiple standalone cards in a single widget.\n\n**Configuration Structure**\n\nlayoutMode (string, optional)\n\n- Controls the card grid layout.\n- Allowed values:\n  - default: preserve the normal responsive layout behavior\n  - collapsed: force two cards per row\n  - single-col: always show one card per row\n- IMPORTANT: default is the normal behavior and should usually be omitted instead of emitted explicitly.\n\ncards (array, required)\n\n- Provide one card metadata object per card.\n- Every card follows the same schema as cardWidget.\n- Keep the top-level oraInfoDisplay title/description shared for the whole set; only card-specific fields belong inside each cards[] entry.\n\nEach cards[] entry supports:\n\n- subject (string, required): clear, concise title\n- subtitle (string, optional): secondary line directly below the title\n- summary (string, required): 1-2 sentences of descriptive text\n- status (string, optional): bottom status text below the summary\n- statusPriority (string, optional): \"alert\", \"warning\", \"medium\", or \"success\"\n- timestamp (string, optional): human-readable relative time\n- badgeText (string, optional): short label for categorization\n- link (object, optional): primary action with text + action\n- additionalLink (object, optional): secondary action with text + action\n- variant (string, optional): \"error\", \"warning\", \"info\", or null\n\n**Important Rules**\n\n- Omit layoutMode unless the prompt explicitly asks for collapsed or single-col behavior.\n- Only use additionalLink when link is also present.\n- If status is present and statusPriority is omitted, the UI will treat it as medium.\n- Keep each card independently scannable.\n- Use multiCardWidget when the user needs several peer cards, not one table or one message list.\n- Do not add actions unless the user explicitly requests interactivity.\n    </instructions>\n    <examples>\n// Example 1: Two simple cards\n{\n    \"cards\": [\n        {\n            \"subject\": \"Pre-pricing alignment\",\n            \"subtitle\": \"ZenBank - Digital Channels Renewal (P1)\",\n            \"summary\": \"Align guardrails and next steps before the March 15 close.\",\n            \"status\": \"Last interaction raised budget concern\",\n            \"statusPriority\": \"warning\",\n            \"timestamp\": \"Today 3:00 PM\",\n            \"badgeText\": \"Today\",\n            \"variant\": \"info\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"subject\": \"Policy Reminder\",\n            \"summary\": \"Expense approvals are due by end of day.\",\n            \"timestamp\": \"Today\",\n            \"badgeText\": \"Reminder\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n// Example 2: Multiple cards with actions\n{\n    \"cards\": [\n        {\n            \"subject\": \"System Alert\",\n            \"subtitle\": \"Web cluster / US-East\",\n            \"summary\": \"High CPU usage detected on web servers. Investigation in progress.\",\n            \"status\": \"Mitigation in progress\",\n            \"statusPriority\": \"alert\",\n            \"timestamp\": \"15 min ago\",\n            \"link\": {\n                \"text\": \"Details\",\n                \"action\": \"view_error_details\"\n            },\n            \"badgeText\": \"Alert\",\n            \"variant\": \"error\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"subject\": \"New Policy Update\",\n            \"subtitle\": \"Corporate travel and expense\",\n            \"summary\": \"Company travel policy has been updated with new guidelines.\",\n            \"status\": \"Review due this week\",\n            \"statusPriority\": \"medium\",\n            \"timestamp\": \"Yesterday\",\n            \"link\": {\n                \"text\": \"View Policy\",\n                \"action\": \"view_policy\"\n            },\n            \"additionalLink\": {\n                \"text\": \"Dismiss\",\n                \"action\": \"dismiss_notification\"\n            },\n            \"badgeText\": \"Policy\",\n            \"variant\": \"warning\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n// Example 3: Explicit single-column layout\n{\n    \"layoutMode\": \"single-col\",\n    \"cards\": [\n        {\n            \"subject\": \"Critical Alert\",\n            \"summary\": \"Database failover triggered in the primary region.\",\n            \"timestamp\": \"5 min ago\",\n            \"badgeText\": \"Critical\",\n            \"variant\": \"error\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"subject\": \"Capacity Warning\",\n            \"summary\": \"API cluster is running above the recommended threshold.\",\n            \"timestamp\": \"12 min ago\",\n            \"badgeText\": \"Warning\",\n            \"variant\": \"warning\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n    </examples>\n</multiCardWidget>"
            }
          },
          "id": "1775957079972",
          "code": "EXECUTION_WIDGET",
          "type": "LLM",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775957079972_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Account Summary Insights."
            },
            {
              "id": "1775957079972_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "DIRECTIVE: Generate exactly one `oraInfoDisplay` block using `patternId: \"multiCardWidget\"` from {{$context.$nodes.ADD_PRODUCTS_SUMMARY.$output}}\n\nROOT CONFIGURATION:\n\n1. Generate a single sentence professional insight using only {{$context.$variables.summaryArray}}.\n\n   * Create a concise headline that highlights interesting, problematic, or traceable entities across the list.\n   * If nothing stands out, generate a single-sentence informational headline.\n\n2. Generate a short summary using only {{$context.$nodes.ADD_PRODUCTS_SUMMARY.$output}}.\n\n   * Write 1 concise sentence describing the most useful and relevant information across the list.\n   * This summary must appear immediately below the heading.\n\nmultiCardWidget Generation Rule:\n\nFor `properties`:\n  - Use `multiCardWidget`\n  - Set `layoutMode` to `\"collapsed\"`\n  - Add `cards` for each row in {{$context.$nodes.ADD_PRODUCTS_SUMMARY.$output}}\n\n Based on {{$context.$nodes.ADD_PRODUCTS_SUMMARY.$output}}, Create the cards as below:\n\n  subject: <map from Subject attribute in each row>\n  subtitle: <Generate 1 line professional short sentence showing the insight>\n  summary: <map from Summary attribute in each row. Display in bullet points format it with markdown>\n  badgeText: <map from BadgeText attribute in each row>\n  variant: <map from Variant attribute in each row>\n\n\nSTRICT CONSTRAINTS:\n\n* Do not use {{$context.$variables.summaryArray}} to populate card fields.\n* Do not modify or rephrase subject, summary, BadgeText, or Variant.\n* Do not add timestamp or any additional properties.\n* Do not generate extra cards.\n* Do not include any additional narrative text before or between cards.\n* Only generate oraInfoDisplay blocks for rows from {{$context.$nodes.ADD_PRODUCTS_SUMMARY.$output}}.\n* Do NOT generate any additional oraInfoDisplay blocks for summaries, context, or {{$context.$variables.summaryArray}}.\n* Do NOT create any \"summary\", \"contextual\", or aggregated card.\n* {{$context.$variables.summaryArray}} must be used only for the heading, summary, and final bullet list.\n\nSTYLE CONSTRAINTS:\n\n* Professional and concise\n* No ALL CAPS\n* No internal field names\n* No technical explanations\n* No repetition\n* Business-friendly language only\n\nFINAL OUTPUT FORMAT:\n\n* Start with the headline\n* Follow with the 1–2 sentence summary\n* Then oraInfoDisplay card block\n* Do not wrap or explain the output"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
