        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Response"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6407,
            "y": 7648
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "id": "1776548407522",
          "code": "GENERATE_RESPONSE",
          "type": "LLM",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776548407522_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use concise and clear language for each output section. Maintain all existing\nprompt template rules and expression formats as provided."
            },
            {
              "id": "1776548407522_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Using the outputs from GET_APPOINTMENT_DETAILS Data - {{$context.$nodes.GET_APPOINTMENT_DETAILS.$output}} and \nGET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING Data - {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output}}, generate a detailed meeting \npreparation summary with the following structure:\n\n## Meeting Preparation\n- Use the 'Subject' field from the first element of GET_APPOINTMENT_DETAILS output. - Mardown header level 1\n- Use the 'detailedAgenda' from GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING node's items[0].payload.what.facts.agenda.detailedAgenda.\n\nTime: <Format 'ActivityStartDate' from GET_APPOINTMENT_DETAILS node into locale date and time with local timezone at end, e.g., \"Jan 20, 2026, Thursday 3:00PM PST\" or \n  \"January 20th, Thursday 3:00PM PST\".>\n- For location, use 'Location' from GET_APPOINTMENT_DETAILS if present; otherwise, use 'ActivityDescription' location if \n  available; if neither, omit location.\n\n#### About <{{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.accountInsights.name}}>\n- Industry: {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.accountInsights.industry}}\n- Sentiment: {{\n  let s = $context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.accountInsights.sentiment;\n  s.charAt(0).toUpperCase()+s.slice(1)+\" sentiment: \" + $context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.accountInsights.sentimentDescription\n}}\n- Products: {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.accountInsights.products}}\n\n\n#### \n{{\n  let opp = $context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.opportunityInsights;\n  let lead = $context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.leadInsights;\n  let data = opp || lead;\n  if(data){\n    let parts = [];\n    if(data.name) parts.push(data.name);\n    if(data.stage) parts.push(data.stage + (data.winProbability ? \"(\" + data.winProbability + \")\" : \"\"));\n    if(data.dealSize) parts.push(data.dealSize);\n    if(data.closeDate) parts.push(data.closeDate);\n    parts.join(\" | \");\n  }\n}} \n\n\n{{\n  let opp = $context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.opportunityInsights;\n  let lead = $context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.leadInsights;\n  let data = opp || lead;\n  if(data){\n    let details = [];\n    if(data.products) details.push(\"Products: \" + data.products);\n    if(data.keyStakeholder) details.push(\"Key Stakeholder: \" + data.keyStakeholder);\n    if(data.signals) details.push(\"Signals: \" + data.signals);\n    if(data.competitiveLandscape) details.push(\"Competitive Landscape: \" + data.competitiveLandscape);\n    details.join(\"\\n- \");\n  }\n}}\n\n#### Customer Attendees\n{{\n  let contacts = $context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.contactRelationship || [];\n  contacts.map(c => {\n    let sentiment = c.sentiment.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + c.sentiment.slice(1) + \" sentiment: \" + c.sentimentDescription;\n    let nameTitle = c.name + (c.jobTitle ? \" (\" + c.jobTitle + \")\" : \"\");\n    let influence = c.influenceLevel.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + c.influenceLevel.slice(1) + \" influence - \" + c.influenceDescription;\n    return `- ${nameTitle}\n  - ${sentiment}\n  - ${influence}\n  - Recent Engagement: ${c.recentEngagement || \"N/A\"}`;\n  }).join(\"\\n\")\n}}\n\n#### Pre-Meeting Checklist\n- {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.meetingStrategyAndRecommendations.preMeetingChecklist.join(\"\\n- \")}}\n\n#### Key Talking Points\n{{\n  let points = $context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.meetingStrategyAndRecommendations.talkingPoints || [];\n  points.map((p,i) => `${i+1}. ${p}`).join(\"\\n\")\n}}\n\n#### Objection Handling\n- {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.meetingStrategyAndRecommendations.objectionHandling.join(\"\\n- \")}}\n\n#### Intended Outcome\n- {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.meetingStrategyAndRecommendations.intendedOutcome.join(\"\\n- \")}}\n\n#### Recent Engagement Summary\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_INSIGHTS_FOR_MEETING.$output.items[0].payload.what.facts.recentEngagementSummary}}\n\nEnsure all markdown formatting is correct and omit any sections or fields if data is missing. Maintain proper spacing between sections without excessive blank lines."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Refine Commercial",
            "sourceCode": "let result = { accountNews: null, companyProfile: null };\ntry {\n  // Access the output from GET_COMPANY_NEWS node\n  const output = $context.$nodes?.GET_COMPANY_NEWS?.$output.items[0];\n  \n  // Access the payload property which is expected to be a JSON string\n  const payloadStr = output?.payload;\n  \n  if (typeof payloadStr === 'string') {\n    // Parse the JSON string safely\n    const payloadObj = JSON.parse(payloadStr);\n    \n    // Safely access nested properties\n    const accountNews = payloadObj?.what?.facts?.accountNews ?? null;\n    const companyProfile = payloadObj?.what?.facts?.companyProfile ?? null;\n    \n    result = { accountNews, companyProfile };\n  }\n} catch (error) {\n  // In case of error, return nulls\n  result = { accountNews: null, companyProfile: null };\n}\n\nreturn result;",
            "returnType": "object"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6881,
            "y": 6982
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775863444348"
          },
          "id": "1776792489554",
          "code": "REFINE_COMMERCIAL",
          "type": "CODE",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summary"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6881,
            "y": 7204
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "id": "1775863444348",
          "code": "SUMMARY",
          "type": "LLM",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775863444348_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Using: {{$context.$variables.insightsArray}} and {{$context.$nodes.REFINE_COMMERCIAL.$output.result}}\nGenerate a concise, professional account insight summary.\n\nInput Guidelines:\n- Each item contains what and why sections\n- Use both sections as the source of truth\n- Treat all insights as belonging to one account\n- Do not output JSON\n- Do not mention internal fields such as schemaVersion, facts, or reasons\n\nOutput Requirements:\n1. Account Title\n- Generate a single, clear title reflecting the overall account situation\n- Consider themes such as risk, renewal posture, expansion potential, or a combination\n- Keep it short, professional, and insight-driven\n- Format as: ## Account Title\n- Include this section only if there is relevant data to generate a meaningful title\n\n2. Consolidated Why Summary\n- Generate a dynamic heading based on dominant themes across all why sections\n- Example: Why this account needs attention\n- Format as: #### Why Heading\n- Write a markdown bullet points of 2 to 3 sentences that synthesizes all why content, removes duplication, and highlights key drivers, signals, and supporting facts\n- Include this section only if why data is present; otherwise omit or generate a valid sentence based on available data\n\n3. Consolidated What Summary\n- Generate a dynamic heading based on dominant themes across all what sections\n- Example: What is happening across the account\n- Format as: #### What Heading\n- Write a markdown bullet points of 2 to 3 markdown bullet points that synthesizes all what content, removes duplication, and highlights key account conditions, risks, and opportunities\n- Include this section only if what data is present; otherwise omit or generate a valid sentence based on available data\n\n4. Additional Sections from REFINE_COMMERCIAL Output\n- For each property in {{$context.$nodes.REFINE_COMMERCIAL.$output.result}} (accountNews, companyProfile):\n  - If the property has value, create a section similar to the What Summary\n  - Generate a dynamic heading reflecting the content, e.g., \"Latest Account News\" or \"Company Profile Overview\"\n  - Write a concise 2 to 3 markdown bullet points synthesizing the content\n  - Format as: #### [Dynamic Heading]\n\nStyle Constraints:\n- Maintain a professional, concise, business tone\n- Avoid repetition across sections\n- Represent the output using markdown bullet points\n- Do not use ALL CAPS\n- Focus on insight synthesis\n\nFinal Output Format:\n- Include each section only if relevant data exists\n- ## Account Title\n- #### Why Heading\n- Represent the output using markdown bullet points\n- #### What Heading\n- Represent the output using markdown bullet points\n- #### Additional Sections as applicable\n- Represent the output using markdown bullet points\n\nIf any section lacks data, omit that section or generate a valid, concise sentence based on available insights."
            },
            {
              "id": "1775863444348_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a concise insight summarization assistant for a Sales Representative in Sales Play."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "1779822892823",
          "code": "PAYLOAD_FOR_OPPORTUNITIES",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Payload for Opportunities",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let result = {};\ntry {\n  const accountNumber = $context.$variables.accountNumber || \"\";\n\n  // Build the payload object as specified\n  result = {\n    entity: \"Opportunity\",\n    fields: [\"OptyId\", \"OptyNumber\"],\n    sort: [\n      {\n        attribute: \"LastUpdateDate\",\n        direction: \"descending\"\n      }\n    ],\n    q: {\n      op: \"$and\",\n      criteria: [\n        {\n          op: \"$eq\",\n          attribute: \"CustomerAccount.PartyNumber\",\n          value: accountNumber\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"$in\",\n          attribute: \"StatusCode\",\n          values: [\"OPEN\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  };\n} catch (error) {\n  // Return empty object on error\n  result = {};\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5010.5,
            "y": 6760
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779822987687"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
